WEBVTT

00:08.633 --> 00:12.095
MEOTO ZENZAI

00:19.728 --> 00:20.562
Dokuga.

00:21.271 --> 00:23.398
Tetsujo. How's Risu?

00:23.898 --> 00:25.400
Well, he's sleeping for now.

00:26.776 --> 00:27.652
All right.

00:30.405 --> 00:32.615
Dokuga... You know, don't you?

00:33.575 --> 00:34.909
You know who killed Risu?

00:36.327 --> 00:40.081
Yeah. I saw him die with my own two eyes.

00:41.249 --> 00:43.084
Then... Who did it?

00:50.550 --> 00:53.344
This letter plane is from Kento.

02:27.230 --> 02:31.651
Boss... We made you your favorite. Please
enjoy it.

02:32.360 --> 02:35.780
I was able to obtain some really
wonderful parts today.

02:39.159 --> 02:43.621
The black powder has run out, and our
organization has weakened significantly.

02:44.455 --> 02:47.167
But this time, we can take advantage of
this woman...

02:50.753 --> 02:52.797
Hey, that smells pretty good!

02:53.965 --> 02:55.175
Ravioli?! Yeah!

02:56.759 --> 02:58.928
- Damn it!
- What the hell's this?

03:06.311 --> 03:07.604
Damn, that's close!

03:09.105 --> 03:11.274
Bastard! Where'd you get that mask?!

03:13.067 --> 03:15.820
As you can see, this mask belonged
to your partner.

03:15.904 --> 03:18.615
Taking you hostage made it really easy to
kill him.

03:20.116 --> 03:23.578
No way... Shin is... he's dead?!

03:30.877 --> 03:31.878
I'll kill you!

03:51.022 --> 03:52.023
B... Boss...

03:53.024 --> 03:53.858
Huh?

03:54.734 --> 03:55.735
Help me...

03:58.404 --> 04:00.698
I don't want... to die...

04:04.369 --> 04:05.495
Help... me...

04:14.879 --> 04:17.173
I don't think Noi's here.

04:19.634 --> 04:23.346
Shin! Aw man, your body's so cold.

04:24.013 --> 04:26.391
Noi... We have to find her...

04:26.474 --> 04:28.142
But I've gotta help you!

04:31.396 --> 04:32.230
Shin, look!

04:36.317 --> 04:37.652
Noi! Are you-

05:15.815 --> 05:18.192
Too slow for me, you giant freak!

05:22.488 --> 05:24.240
Giant transformation magic?

05:32.790 --> 05:36.502
Noi! Okay. You're still alive.

05:37.253 --> 05:41.007
Hey, mister... What are you doing up there?

05:45.011 --> 05:47.096
Oh, wait. This is wax.

05:53.394 --> 05:54.937
Kasukabe! What are you doing?!

05:55.021 --> 05:56.022
Huh?!

05:56.105 --> 05:58.024
It's all collapsing! Get out!

06:13.456 --> 06:15.541
Come... back... boss...

06:21.381 --> 06:22.215
Kasukabe?

06:25.468 --> 06:27.095
Kasukabe... no...

06:29.806 --> 06:32.141
Ouch... ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch...

06:35.812 --> 06:40.775
No way. That... face... It looks
just like him.

06:42.193 --> 06:43.945
But... But, why...

06:50.785 --> 06:51.619
Hayes...

06:52.829 --> 06:53.663
Hayes...

06:54.414 --> 06:55.540
Hayes, wake up.

06:56.124 --> 07:00.002
Who's that? I left that name in the past.

07:00.962 --> 07:02.713
- Wake up.
- Ha... ru...?

07:03.464 --> 07:04.298
Hayes.

07:05.133 --> 07:08.886
It's been quite a while, Hayes. I didn't
recognize you at first because you

07:08.970 --> 07:10.263
look like this.

07:11.097 --> 07:13.266
It's been a while since I woke up
my husband.

07:13.349 --> 07:14.350
What?!

07:15.726 --> 07:18.813
I was flying through the sky and
picked up a nostalgic scent.

07:19.439 --> 07:23.276
I also noticed, it seems you're still
writing books under my name... Professor

07:23.359 --> 07:24.485
Kasukabe.

07:26.279 --> 07:27.530
Haru, you're...

07:28.448 --> 07:33.703
Yeah. I actually became a devil. It had
always been a dream of mine.

07:34.287 --> 07:35.913
So, I took the devil exam.

07:37.123 --> 07:40.751
But I couldn't return to the Hole
looking like this... That was a horrible

07:40.835 --> 07:41.794
thing I did to you.

07:43.921 --> 07:46.924
It's fine.
I'm just glad to know you're alive.

07:47.508 --> 07:49.594
Here, this is yours I believe.

07:53.931 --> 07:55.641
Thank you, Hayes.

08:02.023 --> 08:05.067
What a re- Woah! It all burned to
the ground!

08:05.151 --> 08:07.195
That explains why it felt so
hot in there.

08:07.278 --> 08:08.529
Hey... You guys! Are you both okay?

08:08.613 --> 08:10.323
- Huh?
- Huh?

08:10.865 --> 08:12.575
- Professor!
- Professor!

08:13.993 --> 08:17.205
It's Shin and his partner! Is it
possible? They both died trying

08:17.288 --> 08:18.623
to save us?

08:19.123 --> 08:21.709
They're fine.
Thankfully they're both still alive.

08:22.210 --> 08:25.796
It's a shame. After all we've been
through, you still didn't get to see

08:25.880 --> 08:28.966
- your wife.
- Nah. I did see her.

08:39.560 --> 08:42.522
So tell me, how long have you known about
Nikaido?

08:51.447 --> 08:55.618
Why did you choose to keep "The Sorcerer
Who Can Manipulate Time" hidden from us?

08:56.536 --> 08:58.412
Answer me, Asu.

09:06.879 --> 09:12.426
I doubt that a natural born devil like
you could ever understand, Chidaruma.

09:13.594 --> 09:14.679
Very well.

09:26.107 --> 09:30.987
Oh, come on?! What even is this place?
It's deader than dead around here!

09:31.487 --> 09:35.491
What the hell was he thinking, sending us
here? Stupid pig-face devil!

09:35.992 --> 09:39.620
Caiman, don't you think Asu deliberately
chose a deserted area?

09:40.121 --> 09:42.123
It's game over if En finds us.

09:42.206 --> 09:46.419
Hey, don't forget that magic doesn't work
on me! So I'm not afraid at all!

09:47.420 --> 09:50.923
Yeah, well, Asu said if I were to
meet En now, I'll become his partner

09:51.007 --> 09:53.843
again and you and I will be back to
being enemies.

09:55.678 --> 09:58.723
Well, I for sure don't want you as my
enemy ever again.

09:59.307 --> 10:03.144
If that wasn't enough, that heart-face
bastard is a real pain too.

10:04.145 --> 10:06.188
Asu... I hope you're okay.

10:08.691 --> 10:12.278
- Caiman.
- Ain't this... a subway entrance?

10:14.739 --> 10:15.990
Mas... tema?

10:17.283 --> 10:20.536
Mastema... This is the town where En
fought the Cross-Eyed boss six

10:20.620 --> 10:21.871
years ago.

10:27.752 --> 10:28.919
It's a shopping mall!

10:32.632 --> 10:35.551
Hey, this place feels like the Hole,
don'tcha think?

10:36.052 --> 10:38.554
We might be able to get some weapons and
clothes.

10:38.638 --> 10:41.766
Yeah, but... we don't have any money. So
we'll have to rob people again.

10:41.849 --> 10:43.184
That or shoplift, I guess.

10:44.977 --> 10:49.523
Caiman. Stay alert. There's somebody in
this place trying to follow us.

10:49.607 --> 10:50.441
Really?

10:58.866 --> 11:01.202
Huh? What? Damn it.

11:04.664 --> 11:07.792
Alright, who the hell are you? Why are
you trying to follow us?

11:07.875 --> 11:10.503
W-Wait, no! You don't understand, I'm one
of you!

11:11.003 --> 11:12.630
One of whaa?

11:12.713 --> 11:15.257
Caiman. Let her go.

11:18.594 --> 11:20.513
Aw, man, that hurt! Ouch!

11:21.013 --> 11:22.139
Tell us who you are.

11:23.182 --> 11:25.226
I'm one of you guys! See?

11:27.061 --> 11:29.980
Although I only got it tattooed on
my eye a week ago, heh.

11:33.192 --> 11:36.696
I've never seen either of you around here
before. Are you new to town?

11:37.613 --> 11:41.242
I work for Mr. Maki. I'm one of his
pushers. I'm Natsuki. Well, I guess you

11:41.325 --> 11:43.744
could say I'm more of a rookie dealer.

11:45.121 --> 11:47.081
So you guys came to see Mr. Maki, right?

11:47.164 --> 11:48.124
Huh?

11:48.207 --> 11:49.583
Just play along with her, Caiman.

11:49.667 --> 11:53.337
Aah, yeah! That's right! How's Maki
doing?

11:53.421 --> 11:56.924
Sales really haven't been great lately,
so he's not looking very well.

11:57.007 --> 12:00.970
Oh? Sorry, business calls! Please,
wait here won't you, I'll be right back.

12:07.226 --> 12:09.645
What the hell? What do you think she's
selling?

12:09.729 --> 12:12.273
Thanks for waiting! I'll go and get
Mr. Maki.

12:12.773 --> 12:16.277
Actually. Before you do that, there's
something I want to ask of you.

12:16.360 --> 12:17.194
PAWN

12:17.737 --> 12:20.823
Yo! Old Hag! Sell these people some
weapons and clothes, okay?

12:20.906 --> 12:23.784
- Ooooh!
- Woah! Alright!

12:24.827 --> 12:28.247
According to rumors, some of the
stuff here was actually sold by the

12:28.330 --> 12:30.166
Cross-Eyes boss and his closest men!

12:31.917 --> 12:35.337
Well, take your time and have a look
around. I've got to go to work!

12:37.548 --> 12:41.177
Oh, come on! There's nothing in
this place that fits me, damn it!

12:41.677 --> 12:44.054
I've already made my choice, Caiman!

12:47.224 --> 12:51.020
I need some more time! Come on... Let's
see...

12:52.772 --> 12:56.275
Hey, old hag! What have you got
hidden inside this old wicker trunk?

12:56.358 --> 12:59.945
I don't know. Anything that's not
unpacked is the same as it was sold

13:00.029 --> 13:00.863
to me!

13:01.739 --> 13:02.948
How sloppy.

13:07.495 --> 13:10.873
Mr. Maki! Perfect timing! Some people
came looking for you-

13:12.041 --> 13:15.753
Natsuki! You little shit! You've been
slacking off again!

13:16.754 --> 13:17.588
My bad...

13:18.798 --> 13:21.967
Listen, Natsuki. Things are gonna get
real busy from now on.

13:22.051 --> 13:23.260
Look at this!

13:23.761 --> 13:26.347
We're gonna sell all of this stuff
in Mastema. Kay?

13:28.140 --> 13:30.601
That's black powder?! Where did you get
so much?!

13:32.228 --> 13:34.104
The grains are rough. Mr. Maki...

13:34.605 --> 13:37.817
Aren't you the sharp one? You're right,
this powder's all fake.

13:37.900 --> 13:39.026
Huh?!

13:39.109 --> 13:42.154
The boss has been gone for several
years now, so all the real stuff

13:42.238 --> 13:43.113
has finally run out.

13:43.197 --> 13:46.575
The people in Mastema are idiots,
so they're gonna pay me big bucks

13:46.659 --> 13:47.743
for this crap.

13:47.827 --> 13:51.288
But- You can't! The Cross- Eyes invented
the black powder to help those

13:51.372 --> 13:52.498
who couldn't use magic...

13:52.581 --> 13:56.126
Ha! The only reason people join the
Cross-Eyes is because they want to

13:56.210 --> 13:58.546
make some money. Wasn't that the same
for you?

13:58.629 --> 14:01.507
No! No it's not! I don't care about
the money at all!

14:02.258 --> 14:04.760
There's no way that I'm going to help
you!

14:04.844 --> 14:09.890
Bastard! All the kindness I've shown you
and this is how you repay me?! Natsuki!

14:10.641 --> 14:14.562
Hey, hey, easy buddy! What's going on?

14:15.604 --> 14:18.732
What? Who the hell are you? I've never
seen you here before.

14:19.483 --> 14:23.362
Who the hell am I? That's a
good question, I don't even know!

14:23.863 --> 14:26.866
Wait a minute... Don't tell me you're
one of Dokuga's men!

14:27.658 --> 14:29.994
Are you trying to interfere with my
business--

14:30.619 --> 14:31.453
Huh?

14:34.373 --> 14:36.125
You're a little piece of shit!

14:39.128 --> 14:40.087
I'm gonna kill you!

14:43.966 --> 14:45.259
You wanna fight, do ya?!

15:01.817 --> 15:04.361
Oh, Mr. Maki. I'm sorry for you.

15:05.112 --> 15:08.866
I heard that real Cross-Eyes members are
actually incredible in fights when

15:08.949 --> 15:10.367
they're using knives.

15:10.451 --> 15:12.745
You're strong, so you're the real
deal, right?

15:12.828 --> 15:17.458
I don't know, kid! Just leave me alone
and go home. Quit the Cross-Eyes, too.

15:17.541 --> 15:20.044
No chance! I've just decided that
I'm going to tag along with you!

15:20.127 --> 15:22.421
Then I'll meet the boss one day!

15:22.922 --> 15:25.257
No! No way! You're a pain!

15:25.341 --> 15:28.969
No, don't say that! Please let
me tag along, I'll do whatever you say!

15:29.053 --> 15:30.638
Hey! Nikaido!

15:31.180 --> 15:33.974
You're much better at this than me! Help!

15:34.475 --> 15:37.937
You damn piece of scum you need to
pay me what you owe!

15:47.947 --> 15:49.198
Dokuga. Over there.

15:55.120 --> 15:58.999
Kento... He must've turned into a giant
using the magic from the smoke shop.

15:59.500 --> 16:02.169
Dokuga! This is bad, everyone's dead!

16:07.383 --> 16:10.594
This car belongs to En's cleaners.
That's who took out Kento and

16:10.678 --> 16:12.054
the others.

16:13.305 --> 16:15.140
Damn it! What the hell's going on?

16:15.683 --> 16:17.726
Everything here went up in flames!

16:20.145 --> 16:24.108
Look, you said you had food so that's why
I came over, but all you have is cold

16:24.191 --> 16:25.025
rice!

16:25.109 --> 16:28.570
Aw, come on! It's not all bad, anyway
Nikaido's cooking!

16:28.654 --> 16:31.323
So, tell me. How do we get to
Berith then?

16:32.116 --> 16:35.744
Well, maybe we should take a bus.
We could ride to Zagan City and decide

16:35.828 --> 16:37.121
the next step from there.

16:38.122 --> 16:39.206
Zagan City...?

16:39.790 --> 16:40.624
Food's up!

16:41.625 --> 16:44.128
Omurice with hardly any filling at all!

16:45.379 --> 16:47.006
Simple! Nice!

16:48.048 --> 16:50.509
So. How come you're totally broke,
Big Bro?

16:50.592 --> 16:51.719
I'm not your Big Bro!

16:52.803 --> 16:54.972
Hey, I wanna use your bathroom,
is that okay?

16:55.055 --> 16:56.223
Sure! Over there!

16:59.268 --> 17:00.102
Hey, Big Bro.

17:00.185 --> 17:01.145
Hmm?

17:01.228 --> 17:04.690
So tell me about Nikaido, is she your
partner then? Or your lover?!

17:04.773 --> 17:07.860
Uhh... Well... She's my partner.

17:08.694 --> 17:11.572
Oh... But she's not with the Cross-Eyes, right?

17:12.656 --> 17:16.035
There's not even a trace left of the
wound I got in the church. Did Asu

17:16.118 --> 17:18.203
heal it for me?

17:19.747 --> 17:23.083
Well, either way... It doesn't
answer whoever it was that stabbed me

17:23.167 --> 17:25.002
in the first place.

17:28.505 --> 17:31.383
Oh, by the way... I wanna leave this with
you, Big Bro.

17:31.884 --> 17:33.052
What's that, then?

17:33.135 --> 17:36.930
You're so funny, it's the black powder!
This one is genuine. That's the

17:37.014 --> 17:38.766
very last bag.

17:39.725 --> 17:43.729
If you take this, then even somebody who
can't produce smoke, like me of course,

17:43.812 --> 17:46.482
can become a fully-fledged Sorcerer
really easily!

17:46.565 --> 17:49.526
The boss who invented this stuff
really is something!

17:50.319 --> 17:52.029
THE TRAGIC TALE OF THE CROSS-EYES

17:52.112 --> 17:54.907
I've done it! Our grand mansion is now
complete!

17:54.990 --> 17:56.492
Hey! Ushi! Ton!

17:56.992 --> 17:59.912
Stop messing with the merch from our
side job! What are you gonna do if we

17:59.995 --> 18:01.080
can't sell them?!

18:01.163 --> 18:03.665
What? Come on! This house was built
using the envelopes we already

18:03.749 --> 18:06.043
sweated over to make!

18:06.126 --> 18:07.461
It has a dreamlike charm!

18:07.961 --> 18:11.632
Over here's the kitchen... And the
bathroom is huge, like a spa!

18:11.715 --> 18:15.969
We have three sinks and three toilets, so
there's no more need to fight over them

18:16.053 --> 18:16.887
in the mornings!

18:16.970 --> 18:20.224
I see. So you're finally losing your
grip on reality.

18:20.974 --> 18:23.352
Anyway, Dokuga and Tetsujo are late back.

18:23.852 --> 18:26.355
Isn't today the day we get paid a visit?

18:30.984 --> 18:31.819
Hello!

18:34.822 --> 18:38.534
Oh, look! It's our favorite Landlord!
You're looking as beautiful as ever!

18:39.034 --> 18:43.664
Oh, my! Hearing that from a fine
man like you certainly makes my day!

18:45.791 --> 18:48.377
But let's get straight to business.
I need this month's rent as well

18:48.460 --> 18:51.130
as the last six months you still
haven't paid me yet. Now don't get me

18:51.213 --> 18:53.966
wrong. I like you guys, I really do,
but today's the day you pay what is

18:54.049 --> 18:54.883
owed.

18:58.011 --> 19:01.140
Ah, well, Dokuga will be bringing you the
money soon, in the meantime, Ushishimada

19:01.223 --> 19:03.433
here will keep you company,

19:04.685 --> 19:07.646
Well how can I say no to a wonderful
offer like that?

19:10.149 --> 19:12.693
It's so nice to see you, Ushishimada.

19:12.776 --> 19:14.778
Yeah, you too... missus.

19:15.279 --> 19:17.281
Oh, no, don't call me "missus,"

19:17.364 --> 19:18.949
I'm single, silly!

19:20.325 --> 19:21.577
A visitor? Good.

19:22.077 --> 19:25.747
Why don't you become my partner?
You know, if you do then you won't have

19:25.831 --> 19:27.958
to pay rent for as long as you live here!

19:29.376 --> 19:32.963
And as for those friends of yours?
Not to worry, I'll take care of them

19:33.046 --> 19:33.881
as well!

19:35.841 --> 19:38.594
Although... I'm sure Dokuga will
be back soon.

19:39.386 --> 19:40.804
It's Dokuga and Tetsujo!

19:40.888 --> 19:42.848
What!? Oh, they're back!

19:43.640 --> 19:45.392
Dokuga! We've been waiting for you!

19:46.393 --> 19:47.227
Y'got the cash?

19:50.564 --> 19:53.692
Kento and the others were wiped
out by En's cleaners. The last

19:53.775 --> 19:57.321
black powder the boss made, even
the expensive smoke, all up in flames.

19:57.404 --> 20:01.033
Are you kidding me? So you're telling me
that our entire fortune is just

20:01.116 --> 20:03.202
those envelopes we use for our side job?!

20:04.286 --> 20:06.997
So does that mean we have to leave this
place as well?

20:07.539 --> 20:08.540
- Where's Risu?
- Huh?

20:08.624 --> 20:10.083
You're supposed to watch him.

20:12.252 --> 20:15.839
Damnit! Come on, there's got to be
something here! There must be a clue

20:15.923 --> 20:17.633
about whoever killed me!

20:18.425 --> 20:21.011
So is that your plan? Steal something
from my desk?

20:21.762 --> 20:25.599
Well, bad news for you. You're not
gonna find anything valuable there.

20:26.099 --> 20:29.603
I'm here because you're not telling
me everything! I need to know who

20:29.686 --> 20:31.939
killed me! Did the boss order it?!

20:32.481 --> 20:36.068
Or maybe... It was you, Dokuga.

20:39.696 --> 20:43.742
You know, this isn't the first time we've
had a thief break into this house.

20:44.618 --> 20:48.622
Let me show you... Just exactly what I did
to him when I caught him.

20:49.998 --> 20:53.168
This is it... We're out of money.
We have no choice but to leave,

20:53.252 --> 20:56.630
and each of us go our separate ways.

20:56.713 --> 21:00.676
Damn it! The five of us were supposed to
stay here and wait for the boss to

21:00.759 --> 21:04.304
- return!
- We've lost to poverty.

21:05.055 --> 21:06.640
- Don't worry. Leave it to me.
- Huh?

21:06.723 --> 21:07.557
- Huh?
- Huh?

21:07.641 --> 21:09.518
I will go and live with the Landlord.

21:10.978 --> 21:14.690
If I do that, then the rest of
you can stay here and live rent free!

21:14.773 --> 21:16.066
Don't be an idiot!

21:16.149 --> 21:17.859
As if we'd let you do something
like that!

21:17.943 --> 21:18.777
It's my choice!

21:19.778 --> 21:25.492
So then, if giving myself helps you all...
Then I'll gladly sacrifice myself.

21:26.493 --> 21:27.577
Ushishimada...

21:28.787 --> 21:30.497
You're so incredibly brave...

21:30.580 --> 21:33.333
What's going on out here? Do you have
the money or not?

21:35.043 --> 21:38.463
Landlord... I'm sorry, but we don't.
But I have decided to go with you

21:38.547 --> 21:39.548
instead.

21:40.424 --> 21:41.300
Oh, my!

21:57.065 --> 21:59.234
My eyes! What the hell did you
do to them?!

22:01.570 --> 22:03.196
My saliva is poisonous.

22:17.169 --> 22:20.339
I won't kill you. Because you're too
"dangerous."

22:25.010 --> 22:27.888
This is the deed to the house.
From now on, this building

22:27.971 --> 22:29.848
belongs to you!

22:30.640 --> 22:33.727
Right then. Shall we make our way home,
Ushishimada?

22:35.604 --> 22:39.733
And you know what? That envelope house we
made would have been perfect to call our

22:39.816 --> 22:41.485
home. Farewell.

22:42.027 --> 22:43.028
- Ushishimada!
- Ushishimada!

22:43.111 --> 22:44.613
Ushishimada!

22:57.209 --> 22:58.877
EAST BERITH

23:04.883 --> 23:08.637
Zagan... I'm sure I've heard that name
somewhere before.

23:09.137 --> 23:12.224
Just where on Earth was it?

23:12.307 --> 23:13.683
ZAGAN MAGIC TRAINING SCHOOL

23:17.479 --> 23:22.025
Professor Kasukabe. I became a Sorcerer.

23:23.026 --> 23:23.944
Hey, Kasukabe.

23:24.945 --> 23:27.572
- Huh?
- You spaced out there. Are you okay?

23:28.323 --> 23:29.699
Are you still in some pain?

23:30.283 --> 23:33.995
No... I'm okay, thanks. That wax figure...

23:34.663 --> 23:36.206
- Wax figure?
- Mh-hm...

23:36.706 --> 23:40.419
There was something like an altar,
and right there in the center of it was

23:40.502 --> 23:41.545
this wax figure.

23:42.337 --> 23:44.840
Although unfortunately it melted
in the fire.

23:45.924 --> 23:49.302
By the way. Those guys with the
cross marks on their eyes... Are they

23:49.386 --> 23:50.971
some sort of organization?

23:51.054 --> 23:54.641
Yeah, they're our enemies. We've taken
out quite a few of them, though.

23:54.724 --> 23:57.018
Caiman has that cross mark, as well.

23:57.686 --> 23:58.979
Wha-? Oh yeah!

24:00.856 --> 24:04.067
That is important, but... The face
of that wax figure... It's funny,

24:04.151 --> 24:06.027
but I know him.

24:09.614 --> 24:11.825
Let's go back. To the Hole.

25:41.665 --> 25:42.749
THE END

25:43.250 --> 25:44.751
What we learned in Episode 14.

25:45.252 --> 25:46.878
Kasukabe's wife is a devil.

25:46.962 --> 25:49.297
The guys from the Cross-Eyes are flat
broke.

25:49.381 --> 25:51.132
Zagan exists in Caiman's memories.

25:51.216 --> 25:55.554
What we're going to learn in Episode 15:
It's still... lost in chaos.

25:55.637 --> 25:57.806
This is... Dorohedoro!
